WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:03.060
From Wes Anderson's intern, to painter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:07.620
to chipmunk? Matthew Gray Gubler has&nbsp;
been Hollywood's quirkiest star even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:12.261
before Criminal Minds. Here's a look into&nbsp;
his early days, first role, and beyond.

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:15.660
Though Matthew Gray Gubler is&nbsp;
known as a successful actor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:20.340
he didn't always think of acting as a career.&nbsp;
According to Biography, Gubler studied acting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:24.420
while in high school at the Las Vegas Academy&nbsp;
of Arts because his main interest, filmmaking,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:28.020
wasn't an option. Fortunately for&nbsp;
him, he was naturally talented,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:32.100
and he went on to star in multiple&nbsp;
productions while in school. Gubler said,

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:36.000
"I never thought I'd be making a living&nbsp;
off of acting — it's still kind of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.300
shock for my family and friends to see&nbsp;
my face on TV every Wednesday night."

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:43.320
He eventually graduated from New York&nbsp;
University's Tisch School of the Arts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:47.340
with a degree in film directing, and later&nbsp;
got the opportunity to direct 11 episodes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:52.800
of "Criminal Minds." Fellow Las Vegas natives&nbsp;
and mega music stars The Killers hired Gubler&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:57.180
to direct two of their music videos as well. The&nbsp;
actor helmed The Killers' videos "Don't Shoot Me&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.180 --> 00:01:01.680
Santa" and "Dirt Sledding." When his breakout&nbsp;
show was reaching its final episode, Parade&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:06.120
asked if Gubler was going to continue acting&nbsp;
or go back to directing, to which he replied,

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:10.500
"With everything I've done in every way, I've&nbsp;
always tried to not necessarily give myself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:15.480
a limit or a trajectory, which is how I was&nbsp;
fortunate enough to end up on this TV show. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:18.420
I think for the future, while directing&nbsp;
is still one of my biggest passions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:21.360
everything is my passion, so I&nbsp;
would love to continue acting."

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:26.160
Before he landed his big role on "Criminal&nbsp;
Minds," Matthew Gray Gubler was a successful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:30.420
male model. While still a student in New&nbsp;
York, he was stopped by a model scout with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:34.740
DNA Model Management and was soon modeling&nbsp;
for industry giants like Tommy Hilfiger,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:40.320
Marc Jacobs, and American Eagle, according to TV&nbsp;
Guide. Regarding the whole experience, he joked,

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:43.920
"It was during a time when there were&nbsp;
really emaciated weirdos modeling. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:45.420
wasn't like they were looking for Fabio."

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:49.500
Even though he's been characteristically&nbsp;
self-deprecating about his looks, Gubler was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:54.420
a successful model who walked in fashion shows and&nbsp;
appeared in several print campaigns. According to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.420 --> 00:02:00.420
models.com, he was once ranked in the top 50 male&nbsp;
models, holding the 46th spot. While he's often&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:05.040
recognized for his looks, Gubler has confessed&nbsp;
that he was bullied as a kid. He told Glamour,

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:09.000
"I'm so thankful for every bully I've ever&nbsp;
had. It never affected me, and that's why&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:13.380
I'm so thankful for them. I learned early on&nbsp;
that if anything, it made me stick closer to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:18.060
who I am and not try...it just made me very&nbsp;
solid with who I was. I don't see it like,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:22.440
'poor me.' I was lucky. It taught me a beautiful&nbsp;
lesson, and I'm really grateful for it."

00:02:22.638 --> 00:02:27.570
"All we want in life is for someone&nbsp;
to see us for who we really are."

00:02:27.570 --> 00:02:31.920
Matthew Gray Gubler's first acting credit is&nbsp;
all thanks to Wes Anderson. In an interview&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:36.420
with Glamour, Gubler explained how he came to&nbsp;
meet Anderson through an internship. He shared,

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:40.620
"In order to graduate from film school, we&nbsp;
had to do a semester of interning. I really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:45.120
wanted to intern for Wes because he's one of my&nbsp;
favorite filmmakers and lives in New York and has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:49.980
a production company there. I sent a little weird&nbsp;
DVD of movies I made and a note saying I would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:54.840
love to get him coffee. I lucked out and got to&nbsp;
work there, and that was a real dream come true."

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:58.980
During his internship, Anderson convinced&nbsp;
Gubler to audition for his upcoming movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:02.460
"The Life Aquatic with Steve Zissou,"&nbsp;
where he ironically played the part&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:06.180
of Intern #1. Shortly after landing&nbsp;
the role, he took a trip to Hollywood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:10.334
and auditioned for a certain crime&nbsp;
procedural show. The rest is history.

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:16.140
Aside from his passions of acting and filmmaking,&nbsp;
Matthew Gray Gubler is a talented artist. In 2004,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:19.440
he created a website that featured&nbsp;
his characteristically quirky art&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:23.640
and for years it served as a sort of&nbsp;
art portfolio for his watercolor, oil,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:28.140
and pastel paintings. He took the webpage down&nbsp;
after Flash was removed from the internet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:30.900
but he's since revitalized&nbsp;
his website with a new look.

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:33.780
Gubler's art has appeared&nbsp;
in galleries, group shows,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:37.020
and magazines, according to The&nbsp;
Things. However, he has confessed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:41.640
he gets nervous when people critique his&nbsp;
art in person. In 2013, he told Buzzfeed,

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:45.960
"On the internet, it's this safe space where I&nbsp;
can put it up and people can click on it or not.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:49.920
I don't have to be in the same room as them&nbsp;
pretending to like it, so I very rarely show&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:54.060
people things ... some people misinterpret&nbsp;
my style of painting as offensive, and I've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:57.540
had instances where I've painted beautiful&nbsp;
portraits for, like, a girlfriend or someone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:01.080
and they're just like, they look at it with a&nbsp;
grimace and they're like, 'This is terrible.'"

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:04.920
Despite his insecurities, his pieces&nbsp;
have sold for thousands of dollars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:09.360
inspired countless tattoos, and received&nbsp;
praise all across the internet. Gubler&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:14.222
may be modest about his skill, but at least the&nbsp;
rest of the world recognizes his many talents.

00:04:14.222 --> 00:04:19.200
In 2007, Matthew Gray Gubler took a reprieve&nbsp;
from the dark world of "Criminal Minds" to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:23.460
provide the voice of Simon –- the loveable,&nbsp;
nerdy brother of Alvin –- in the feature film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:28.320
version of "Alvin and the Chipmunks." According&nbsp;
to Box Office Mojo, the movie would go on to earn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:34.440
an impressive $365 million at the global box&nbsp;
office. Distributed by 20th Century Fox and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:39.420
helmed by "Muppets from Space" director Tim Hill,&nbsp;
"Alvin and the Chipmunks" combines live action&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:45.000
and computer-generated animation to bring the&nbsp;
beloved 1980s cartoon to life. The story centers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:49.560
on three chipmunk brothers adopted by human&nbsp;
songwriter Dave Seville. Gubler's character,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:54.361
Simon, is often the voice of reason among&nbsp;
his mischievous brothers Alvin and Theodore.

00:04:54.361 --> 00:04:56.161
"I feel like I'm living in a dumpster."

00:04:57.267 --> 00:05:00.780
The actor continued to voice Simon&nbsp;
through three more "Chipmunks" films:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:04.560
"The Squeakquel," "Chipwrecked," and "The&nbsp;
Road Chip." The sequel earned even more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:09.420
than its predecessor, raking in $443&nbsp;
million, per Box Office Mojo. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.420 --> 00:05:13.740
the third and fourth films didn't fare quite as&nbsp;
well and there's no word on a fifth movie. In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:18.000
an interview with Page Six, Gubler reflected&nbsp;
on how much he loved playing Simon. He said,

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:22.500
"Oddly, I feel more a part of this than anything&nbsp;
else I've been lucky enough to be in [...] Actors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:26.922
talk about dreaming of playing Othello, but for&nbsp;
me, it's Simon. It's the biggest deal to me."

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:32.640
When "500 Days of Summer" was released in 2009, it&nbsp;
stood apart from its romantic-comedy counterparts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:35.760
specifically because the romance at&nbsp;
the center of the film doesn't last.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:40.320
The film centers on 20-somethings Tom and&nbsp;
Summer as they fall in and out of love.

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:43.800
Matthew Gray Gubler co-stars in&nbsp;
the film as Tom's friend, Paul,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.800 --> 00:05:47.460
who is in a healthy relationship with&nbsp;
a girl named Robyn. He speaks the truth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.460 --> 00:05:50.760
about real love to Tom and comforts&nbsp;
his friend after Summer dumps him.

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:59.280
"But truthfully, Robyn is better than&nbsp;
the girl of my dreams ... She's real."

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:03.600
Although Gubler only appears in a few scenes,&nbsp;
Paul's perspective on love helps illustrate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:07.980
how unrealistic Tom is about romance. In an&nbsp;
article about the film's 10th anniversary,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.980 --> 00:06:12.000
The Observer noted the one-dimensional&nbsp;
characterization of Summer and said of the movie,

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:16.920
"For a film that was heralded as a quirky response&nbsp;
to the traditional romance and has since endured&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:21.180
as a cult classic, its central message and&nbsp;
themes don't go down quite as easily today."

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:25.500
The article further broke down Summer's&nbsp;
lack of character depth and decried her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:28.860
existence as serving no purpose&nbsp;
aside from Tom's dreams. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:33.163
this is the important truth Gubler's&nbsp;
character subtly points out in the film.

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:38.760
The extremely dark 2008 comedy "How to Be&nbsp;
a Serial Killer" allows Matthew Gray Gubler&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.760 --> 00:06:42.720
to portray a wannabe murderer rather&nbsp;
than a profiler and hunter of serial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:47.280
killers. Gubler plays Bart — a nebbish video&nbsp;
store clerk who becomes a student of Mike,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:51.960
a self-help bro with 10 easy steps&nbsp;
to self-actualization via grisly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.960 --> 00:06:57.420
murder. Mike is a dark, twisted Mr. Miyagi to&nbsp;
Bart's Daniel LaRusso and Gubler plays Bart&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.420 --> 00:07:02.040
with believable cowardice. As a review of the&nbsp;
film from horror website Dread Central notes,

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:04.980
"Bart's the kind of character most&nbsp;
audience members will want to beat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:08.520
with a sock full of quarters until he&nbsp;
stops being such a simpering idiot."

00:07:08.520 --> 00:07:13.140
An independent film, "How to Be a Serial&nbsp;
Killer" was distributed by Monterey Media&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:17.100
and only opened on one domestic theater&nbsp;
screen. According to Box Office Mojo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:23.400
the movie played for one weekend and earned $899.&nbsp;
Limited audience reviews of the film on Rotten&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:27.960
Tomatoes were less than favorable. However, Liz,&nbsp;
a super reviewer on the site, called the movie,

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:30.840
"An entertaining social etiquette&nbsp;
of sorts that makes you laugh,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:34.920
creeps you out and makes you want to become&nbsp;
best friends with Matthew Gray Gubler."

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:39.840
Matthew Gray Gubler doesn't usually live his&nbsp;
romances in the limelight. The actor's love&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:44.280
life isn't the focus of his interviews or press&nbsp;
junkets. Nonetheless, like many other Hollywood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.280 --> 00:07:49.860
celebrities, he is rumored to have dated Taylor&nbsp;
Swift, per Cosmopolitan. However, Gubler has never&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:54.660
spoken on the record about a former relationship&nbsp;
with the mega pop star. Kat Dennings remains the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:59.400
one celebrity Gubler has confirmed dating and over&nbsp;
the years, the two have worked on-screen together.

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:04.020
Dennings and Gubler hooked up in 2007&nbsp;
and although their romance didn't last,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:08.460
their friendship has continued in the years&nbsp;
since. The two appeared together in both the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:12.720
small independent horror-comedy "Suburban&nbsp;
Gothic" and the short-lived Hulu series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:16.020
"Dollface." Gubler sat down&nbsp;
with the website Shock Ya to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.020 --> 00:08:19.440
discuss "Suburban Gothic" and his&nbsp;
relationship with Dennings, saying,

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:22.260
"I love Kat, as she's actually&nbsp;
one of my closest friends,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.260 --> 00:08:26.640
and we actually dated many years ago. It's very&nbsp;
rare to find weirdos who are like yourself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.640 --> 00:08:28.740
so when you find them, you keep them close."

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:33.720
The imaginative comedy series "Dollface"&nbsp;
ran for two seasons on Hulu. The show&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:36.960
centered on Dennings character, web&nbsp;
designer Jules Wiley and her search&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.960 --> 00:08:41.901
for love and purpose. Gubler co-starred&nbsp;
as Wes, Jules' potential love interest.

00:08:42.180 --> 00:08:46.380
After Matthew Gray Gubler began to gain&nbsp;
public recognition for his role as Dr.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.380 --> 00:08:51.600
Spencer Reid in "Criminal Minds," he poked&nbsp;
fun at his newfound celebrity status. In 2006,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.600 --> 00:08:57.540
Gubler launched a YouTube series called "Matthew&nbsp;
Gray Gubler: The Unauthorized Documentary" – an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.540 --> 00:09:02.700
obviously satirical episodic series. The actor's&nbsp;
humorous commentary on narcissistic celebrities&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:07.320
who take themselves too seriously pre-dates&nbsp;
the similarly themed Joaquin Phoenix vehicle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.320 --> 00:09:12.300
"I'm Still Here." Although both parodies mock&nbsp;
celebrity culture, Phoenix did extensive press for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.300 --> 00:09:16.920
"I'm Still Here" in character. Phoenix infamously&nbsp;
appeared as his self-absorbed character on "The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:21.723
Late Show with David Letterman" which prompted the&nbsp;
actor to apologize to Letterman 18 months later.

00:09:21.723 --> 00:09:25.499
"But I apologize. I hope I&nbsp;
didn't offend you in any way."

00:09:25.499 --> 00:09:26.401
"No, no, no."

00:09:26.401 --> 00:09:30.960
"I'm Still Here" could almost qualify as serious&nbsp;
performance art, whereas Gubler's video series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:35.700
delights in its silliness. Gubler's YouTube&nbsp;
series spans 14 short episodes, each episode&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:40.500
running under 10 minutes, throughout two seasons&nbsp;
and features guest appearances. In Season 1,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:45.960
Episode 11, the late, great Anton Yelchin takes&nbsp;
acting lessons from Gubler. MTV News points out,

00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:50.000
"[Gubler] has a wonderful sense of humor&nbsp;
and isn't afraid to make fun of himself."

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:55.328
"If we can't shoot the last scene, they can't&nbsp;
end the show, and I don't want the show to end."

00:09:55.328 --> 00:10:01.501
We couldn't agree more. Season 2 of "The&nbsp;
Unauthorized Documentary" aired from 2020 to 2021.

00:10:01.501 --> 00:10:04.620
When the "Criminal Minds" reboot&nbsp;
was announced, the show's fans grew&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:08.760
excited at the return of their favorite&nbsp;
FBI profilers. Before "Criminal Minds:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.760 --> 00:10:12.960
Evolution" premiered, Deadline announced&nbsp;
the return of many long-time stars. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:17.880
glaringly missing from the cast announcement&nbsp;
was Matthew Gray Gubler as Dr. Spencer Reid.

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:23.820
Over 15 seasons, Gubler appeared in 323 of the&nbsp;
original "Criminal Minds" episodes. The actor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.820 --> 00:10:26.100
who began his trajectory&nbsp;
on the show when he was 25,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:30.780
wrapped the series finale when he was&nbsp;
40. Both Gubler and Reid grew up through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.780 --> 00:10:34.800
the show's lengthy run. In an exclusive&nbsp;
interview with Looper, Gubler's friend&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:39.420
and co-star Paget Brewster opened up about&nbsp;
his absence from the reboot. She explained,

00:10:39.420 --> 00:10:41.880
"Matthew was the only person&nbsp;
in the last two seasons that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.880 --> 00:10:45.660
had been in every single episode.&nbsp;
He did 15 years straight through."

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:49.560
She elaborated on Gubler's choice to&nbsp;
decline reprising his role, adding,

00:10:49.560 --> 00:10:52.320
"He was never able to go do&nbsp;
other stuff, so I understand."

00:10:52.320 --> 00:10:55.980
However, Gubler's character hasn't&nbsp;
been killed off of "Criminal Minds:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.980 --> 00:10:59.340
Evolution," and there are numerous&nbsp;
plausible explanations for Reid's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.340 --> 00:11:03.134
absence. Perhaps Gubler will make&nbsp;
guest appearances in future episodes.

